{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"function _safeMint|checkOnERC721Received\\\" packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/utils/ERC721Utils.sol; nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol | sed -n '295,340p'; nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/utils/ERC721Utils.sol | sed -n '15,70p'\"","aggregated_output":"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:135:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), from, to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:279:    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:287:    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal virtual {\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:289:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), address(0), to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol:362:        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), from, to, tokenId, data);\npackages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/utils/ERC721Utils.sol:25:    function checkOnERC721Received(\n   295\t     * This is an internal function that does not check if the sender is authorized to operate on the token.\n   296\t     *\n   297\t     * Requirements:\n   298\t     *\n   299\t     * - `tokenId` must exist.\n   300\t     *\n   301\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   302\t     */\n   303\t    function _burn(uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   304\t        address previousOwner = _update(address(0), tokenId, address(0));\n   305\t        if (previousOwner == address(0)) {\n   306\t            revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   307\t        }\n   308\t    }\n   309\t\n   310\t    /**\n   311\t     * @dev Transfers `tokenId` from `from` to `to`.\n   312\t     *  As opposed to {transferFrom}, this imposes no restrictions on msg.sender.\n   313\t     *\n   314\t     * Requirements:\n   315\t     *\n   316\t     * - `to` cannot be the zero address.\n   317\t     * - `tokenId` token must be owned by `from`.\n   318\t     *\n   319\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   320\t     */\n   321\t    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   322\t        if (to == address(0)) {\n   323\t            revert ERC721InvalidReceiver(address(0));\n   324\t        }\n   325\t        address previousOwner = _update(to, tokenId, address(0));\n   326\t        if (previousOwner == address(0)) {\n   327\t            revert ERC721NonexistentToken(tokenId);\n   328\t        } else if (previousOwner != from) {\n   329\t            revert ERC721IncorrectOwner(from, tokenId, previousOwner);\n   330\t        }\n   331\t    }\n   332\t\n   333\t    /**\n   334\t     * @dev Safely transfers `tokenId` token from `from` to `to`, checking that contract recipients\n   335\t     * are aware of the ERC-721 standard to prevent tokens from being forever locked.\n   336\t     *\n   337\t     * `data` is additional data, it has no specified format and it is sent in call to `to`.\n   338\t     *\n   339\t     * This internal function is like {safeTransferFrom} in the sense that it invokes\n   340\t     * {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} on the receiver, and can be used to e.g.\n    15\t */\n    16\tlibrary ERC721Utils {\n    17\t    /**\n    18\t     * @dev Performs an acceptance check for the provided `operator` by calling {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received}\n    19\t     * on the `to` address. The `operator` is generally the address that initiated the token transfer (i.e. `msg.sender`).\n    20\t     *\n    21\t     * The acceptance call is not executed and treated as a no-op if the target address doesn't contain code (i.e. an EOA).\n    22\t     * Otherwise, the recipient must implement {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} and return the acceptance magic value to accept\n    23\t     * the transfer.\n    24\t     */\n    25\t    function checkOnERC721Received(\n    26\t        address operator,\n    27\t        address from,\n    28\t        address to,\n    29\t        uint256 tokenId,\n    30\t        bytes memory data\n    31\t    ) internal {\n    32\t        if (to.code.length > 0) {\n    33\t            try IERC721Receiver(to).onERC721Received(operator, from, tokenId, data) returns (bytes4 retval) {\n    34\t                if (retval != IERC721Receiver.onERC721Received.selector) {\n    35\t                    // Token rejected\n    36\t                    revert IERC721Errors.ERC721InvalidReceiver(to);\n    37\t                }\n    38\t            } catch (bytes memory reason) {\n    39\t                if (reason.length == 0) {\n    40\t                    // non-IERC721Receiver implementer\n    41\t                    revert IERC721Errors.ERC721InvalidReceiver(to);\n    42\t                } else {\n    43\t                    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n    44\t                        revert(add(reason, 0x20), mload(reason))\n    45\t                    }\n    46\t                }\n    47\t            }\n    48\t        }\n    49\t    }\n    50\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
