{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC721/ERC721.sol | sed -n '268,294p'\"","aggregated_output":"   268\t\n   269\t    /**\n   270\t     * @dev Mints `tokenId`, transfers it to `to` and checks for `to` acceptance.\n   271\t     *\n   272\t     * Requirements:\n   273\t     *\n   274\t     * - `tokenId` must not exist.\n   275\t     * - If `to` refers to a smart contract, it must implement {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received}, which is called upon a safe transfer.\n   276\t     *\n   277\t     * Emits a {Transfer} event.\n   278\t     */\n   279\t    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId) internal {\n   280\t        _safeMint(to, tokenId, \"\");\n   281\t    }\n   282\t\n   283\t    /**\n   284\t     * @dev Same as {xref-ERC721-_safeMint-address-uint256-}[`_safeMint`], with an additional `data` parameter which is\n   285\t     * forwarded in {IERC721Receiver-onERC721Received} to contract recipients.\n   286\t     */\n   287\t    function _safeMint(address to, uint256 tokenId, bytes memory data) internal virtual {\n   288\t        _mint(to, tokenId);\n   289\t        ERC721Utils.checkOnERC721Received(_msgSender(), address(0), to, tokenId, data);\n   290\t    }\n   291\t\n   292\t    /**\n   293\t     * @dev Destroys `tokenId`.\n   294\t     * The approval is cleared when the token is burned.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":false,\"stub_explanation\":\"\",\"results\":[{\"flow_summary\":\"A nested contract call to enableRefunds while another nonReentrant Raffle operation holds the shared guard is rejected before any lifecycle or deadline checks execute.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - external selector dispatch applies the inherited nonReentrant modifier before entering the function body.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:69 ReentrancyGuard.nonReentrant - invokes the pre-entry guard check.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:94 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBefore - checks the shared guard slot before marking the call entered.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:90 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantBeforeView - an already-entered slot terminates the nested call with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall before executing enableRefunds; the nested call makes no state change or event emission.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol\",\"flow_line\":90,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"A contract caller controls whether it issues the zero-argument selector from a callback while another guarded Raffle frame is active. Its address, calldata-free call, and block time do not reach the function body once the guard rejects it.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This is the entrypoint's first security boundary. It prevents callback-driven nested refund activation while another guarded operation is handling accounting or an external asset call.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"While an Active raffle has sold no entries and is still before endTime, only the configured sponsor can close it. The call moves the canonically zero unsettled pot into refund liability, changes status to Refunding, emits RefundsEnabled, and returns normally.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the zero-argument external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Active lifecycle branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:280 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the empty-raffle branch because totalEntries is zero.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:281 Raffle.enableRefunds - loads endTime as the applicable deadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:282 Raffle.enableRefunds - msg.sender equal to sponsor defeats the compound rejection condition even though block.timestamp is before endTime.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:296 Raffle.enableRefunds - snapshots unsettledPot as the liability; reachable accounting invariants make it zero when no entries were sold.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:297 Raffle.enableRefunds - clears unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:298 Raffle.enableRefunds - records the snapshot in remainingRefundLiability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:299 Raffle.enableRefunds - changes the terminal lifecycle to Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:300 Raffle.enableRefunds - emits RefundsEnabled with the sponsor as finalizer and the liability amount.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:105 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - releases the guard before the empty-data return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Commit status Refunding and the pot-to-refund-liability accounting transition, emit RefundsEnabled, then return no data.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":282,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller supplies no calldata. Its msg.sender must equal the stored sponsor, while transaction inclusion timing supplies block.timestamp below endTime. The authorized caller address then reaches RefundsEnabled.finalizer; it does not control the stored liability amount.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 282 is the sponsor-only early-cancellation boundary. It permits closing an escrowed-prize raffle before the public deadline and enables later prize recovery, so sponsor identity enforcement is security-critical.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"Once an empty Active raffle reaches endTime, any EOA or contract may close it. The function records the canonically zero refund liability, changes status to Refunding, emits the caller as finalizer, and returns.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the zero-argument external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Active lifecycle branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:280 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the empty-raffle branch because totalEntries is zero.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:281 Raffle.enableRefunds - loads endTime as the public deadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:282 Raffle.enableRefunds - at block.timestamp greater than or equal to endTime, the compound rejection condition is false regardless of caller identity.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:296 Raffle.enableRefunds - snapshots the canonically zero unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:297 Raffle.enableRefunds - clears unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:298 Raffle.enableRefunds - assigns the snapshot to remainingRefundLiability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:299 Raffle.enableRefunds - changes status to Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:300 Raffle.enableRefunds - emits RefundsEnabled with msg.sender as finalizer.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:105 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - releases the guard before the empty-data return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Commit the empty raffle's Refunding state, emit RefundsEnabled, and return no data.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":282,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller supplies no calldata and may have any identity. Transaction inclusion at block.timestamp greater than or equal to stored endTime opens the path, and msg.sender is written only to the event's finalizer field.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 282 makes empty-raffle closure permissionless at the inclusive sale deadline. This boundary must align with the entry-sale cutoff because the transition permanently disables further sales and enables later prize return.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A non-sponsor attempting to close an empty Active raffle before endTime is rejected at the sponsor/time authorization boundary.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Active branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:280 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the zero-entry branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:281 Raffle.enableRefunds - sets the applicable deadline to endTime.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:282 Raffle.enableRefunds - both msg.sender not equal to sponsor and block.timestamp below endTime make the rejection condition true.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:283 Raffle.enableRefunds - reverts with RefundsNotAvailable(endTime, block.timestamp).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with RefundsNotAvailable; all guard bookkeeping rolls back and raffle accounting, status, and logs remain unchanged.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":282,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller-controlled identity is not the stored sponsor and its transaction is included before endTime. The inclusion timestamp reaches the custom-error payload; there are no calldata arguments.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This authorization check prevents an arbitrary party from terminating an empty raffle while its sale is still open.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an Active raffle with sold entries, any call before endTime plus the two-day draw-request timeout is rejected. The sponsor receives no early override after entries exist.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Active branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:280 Raffle.enableRefunds - totalEntries is nonzero, so execution selects the sold-raffle branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:286 Raffle.enableRefunds - obtains the applicable deadline from drawRequestDeadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:33 RaffleConstants.DRAW_REQUEST_TIMEOUT - supplies the fixed two-day draw-request window.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:458 Raffle.drawRequestDeadline - computes uint256(endTime) plus DRAW_REQUEST_TIMEOUT.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:287 Raffle.enableRefunds - block.timestamp below that deadline causes RefundsNotAvailable(deadline, block.timestamp).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with RefundsNotAvailable; no refund liability, status change, or event is committed.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":287,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Transaction inclusion timing supplies a block.timestamp below the computed deadline and reaches the error payload. Caller identity is irrelevant on the sold-raffle branch, and there are no calldata arguments.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 287 protects both the remaining sale period and the post-sale permissionless draw-request window from premature conversion of ticket-sale proceeds into refunds.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"For an Active raffle with sold entries, any caller may enable full refunds at or after endTime plus two days when no draw was requested. The entire unsettled pot becomes refund liability and status becomes Refunding.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the zero-argument external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Active lifecycle branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:280 Raffle.enableRefunds - totalEntries is nonzero, selecting the sold-raffle branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:286 Raffle.enableRefunds - obtains the public timeout from drawRequestDeadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:33 RaffleConstants.DRAW_REQUEST_TIMEOUT - supplies the fixed two-day timeout.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:458 Raffle.drawRequestDeadline - computes uint256(endTime) plus DRAW_REQUEST_TIMEOUT.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:287 Raffle.enableRefunds - block.timestamp greater than or equal to the computed deadline passes the permissionless gate.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:296 Raffle.enableRefunds - snapshots all unsettled ticket-sale proceeds as liability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:297 Raffle.enableRefunds - clears unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:298 Raffle.enableRefunds - installs the full snapshot as remainingRefundLiability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:299 Raffle.enableRefunds - changes status to Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:300 Raffle.enableRefunds - emits RefundsEnabled with msg.sender and the liability.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:105 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - releases the guard before return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Atomically reclassify the full unsettled pot as ticket-refund liability, enter Refunding, emit RefundsEnabled, and return no data.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":287,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Any caller identity is accepted. Transaction inclusion timing must produce block.timestamp greater than or equal to endTime plus two days; msg.sender reaches the finalizer event field, while the liability amount comes only from stored unsettledPot.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 287 is the permissionless liveness boundary guarding the financial mutations at lines 296-299. It complements requestDraw's exclusive deadline and determines when any party may redirect the full sales pot from draw settlement to refunds.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"While a raffle is Drawing and the accepted VRF request's two-day callback window remains open, any attempt to enable refunds is rejected.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - status is not Active, so execution continues to the next lifecycle check.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:289 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Drawing branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:290 Raffle.enableRefunds - obtains the applicable deadline from callbackDeadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:36 RaffleConstants.DRAW_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT - supplies the fixed two-day callback window.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:464 Raffle.callbackDeadline - for a recorded request, computes uint256(drawRequestedAt) plus DRAW_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:291 Raffle.enableRefunds - block.timestamp below the callback deadline causes RefundsNotAvailable(deadline, block.timestamp).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with RefundsNotAvailable; Drawing status and the unsettled pot remain unchanged for the pending callback.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":291,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"The caller may have any identity, but its transaction is included before the stored request's callback deadline. The inclusion timestamp reaches the custom-error payload; no calldata argument exists.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 291 preserves the authenticated VRF callback's resolution window and prevents a public caller from switching a live draw to refunds prematurely.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"At or after a Drawing raffle's callback deadline, any caller may abandon the timed-out draw and enable full refunds. The full unsettled pot becomes refund liability and the status change causes any later VRF callback to be ignored by the separate callback handler.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the zero-argument external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - status is not Active.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:289 Raffle.enableRefunds - selects the Drawing branch.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:290 Raffle.enableRefunds - obtains the callback deadline.\",\"packages/contracts/src/libraries/RaffleConstants.sol:36 RaffleConstants.DRAW_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT - supplies the fixed two-day timeout.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:464 Raffle.callbackDeadline - computes uint256(drawRequestedAt) plus DRAW_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:291 Raffle.enableRefunds - block.timestamp greater than or equal to the deadline passes the permissionless timeout gate.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:296 Raffle.enableRefunds - snapshots the unsettled sales pot as refund liability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:297 Raffle.enableRefunds - clears unsettledPot.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:298 Raffle.enableRefunds - records the full snapshot as remainingRefundLiability.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:299 Raffle.enableRefunds - changes status from Drawing to Refunding.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:300 Raffle.enableRefunds - emits RefundsEnabled with the caller and liability.\",\"packages/contracts/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/ReentrancyGuard.sol:105 ReentrancyGuard._nonReentrantAfter - releases the guard before return.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Atomically abandon the timed-out Drawing state, reclassify the pot as refund liability, emit RefundsEnabled, and return no data.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":291,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Any caller identity is accepted. Transaction inclusion timing must produce block.timestamp greater than or equal to drawRequestedAt plus two days; msg.sender reaches only the event's finalizer field, while stored unsettledPot determines the liability.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Line 291 is the liveness boundary between accepting randomness and refunding participants. Its inclusive cutoff protects the accounting transition at lines 296-299 and aligns with fulfillRandomWords rejecting callbacks at or after the same deadline.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"Calling enableRefunds while the raffle is AwaitingPrize is rejected before any accounting mutation, preventing refund activation before prize escrow has activated the raffle.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - AwaitingPrize does not match Active.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:289 Raffle.enableRefunds - AwaitingPrize does not match Drawing.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:293 Raffle.enableRefunds - reverts with InvalidStatus(AwaitingPrize).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with InvalidStatus(AwaitingPrize); no status, accounting, or event change survives.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":293,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Caller identity and transaction timing do not affect this branch or its payload. The zero-argument call merely triggers validation, and the stored AwaitingPrize status is encoded in the error.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"The lifecycle gate prevents refund mode and later prize-release eligibility from being established before the configured prize has been accepted into escrow.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"Calling enableRefunds after the raffle has resolved to NftWon or CashWon is rejected, regardless of whether winning-ticket settlement has subsequently allocated the pot.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - NftWon or CashWon does not match Active.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:289 Raffle.enableRefunds - the resolved status does not match Drawing.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:293 Raffle.enableRefunds - reverts with InvalidStatus carrying the resolved status.\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with InvalidStatus(NftWon) or InvalidStatus(CashWon); the selected winner and existing pot or claim allocations remain intact.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":293,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Caller identity and transaction timing cannot bypass the lifecycle check. The caller supplies no arguments; the stored resolved status is the only value encoded in the terminal error.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"This gate prevents a permissionless caller from overturning an authenticated VRF result or replacing already allocated winner, sponsor, and protocol claims with refund accounting.\"},{\"flow_summary\":\"A repeated call after status is already Refunding is rejected instead of reinitializing refund accounting.\",\"flow_trace\":[\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:276 Raffle.enableRefunds - the external call enters under the nonReentrant guard.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:279 Raffle.enableRefunds - Refunding does not match Active.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:289 Raffle.enableRefunds - Refunding does not match Drawing.\",\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol:293 Raffle.enableRefunds - reverts with InvalidStatus(Refunding).\"],\"flow_terminal_action\":\"Revert with InvalidStatus(Refunding); the current remainingRefundLiability, including any prior ticket refunds, is preserved.\",\"flow_file_path\":\"packages/contracts/src/Raffle.sol\",\"flow_line\":293,\"flow_input_to_sink\":\"Caller identity and timing are irrelevant once status is Refunding. The zero-argument call reaches a custom error containing only the stored status.\",\"flow_security_relevance\":\"Rejecting repeat execution is financially important because the successful body assigns remainingRefundLiability from unsettledPot. Once refunds are active, that pot is zero, so the lifecycle gate prevents an outstanding or partially depleted refund liability from being overwritten.\"}]}"}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":324547,"cached_input_tokens":284672,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17068,"reasoning_output_tokens":12029}}
